    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d908">

                <pb facs="0783" n="771" xml:id="pg771"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.011/427</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Messersmith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 373</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-05">June 5, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received June 6.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With further reference to the transitory
                    provision to terminate the moratoria, I have the honor to report that the
                    Constituent Assembly yesterday promulgated the provision, and it is therefore in
                    effect. A copy and translation of the text, as published in the local press, are
                        enclosed.<anchor n="56" xml:id="d908-f1"/></p>
                <p>Certain last-minute changes have been noted. For example, public service
                    corporations are excluded from the benefits of the provision, except those with
                    a capital of less than 100,000 pesos and which are not subsidiaries of larger
                    companies. Railroads, on the other hand, will enjoy the benefits of the
                    provision.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George S.
                    Messersmith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
